   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Definitions",
     "md": "$\\text{sinh}\\, x=\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}$, $\\text{cosh}\\, x=\\frac{e^x+e^{-x}}{2}$, $\\text{tanh}\\, x=\\frac{\\text{sinh}\\, x}{\\text{cosh}\\, x}$. $\\text{cosh}\\,$ is even with minimum value 1 at $x=0$; $\\text{sinh}\\,$ is odd and increasing. 'Hyperbolic' because $(x,y)=(\\text{cosh}\\, t,\\text{sinh}\\, t)$ lies on the hyperbola $x^2-y^2=1$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "propriete",
     "title": "Identities and derivatives",
     "md": "$\\text{cosh}\\,^2x-\\text{sinh}\\,^2x=1$ (compare Osborn's rule: change the sign of each product of two sinh terms in the trigonometric identity). $\\text{sinh}\\,2x=2\\text{sinh}\\, x\\text{cosh}\\, x$, $\\text{cosh}\\,2x=\\text{cosh}\\,^2x+\\text{sinh}\\,^2x=2\\text{cosh}\\,^2x-1$. Derivatives: $\\frac{d}{dx}\\text{sinh}\\, x=\\text{cosh}\\, x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}\\text{cosh}\\, x=\\text{sinh}\\, x$, $\\frac{d}{dx}\\text{tanh}\\, x=\\frac{1}{\\text{cosh}\\,^2x}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Inverse functions",
     "md": "$\\text{arsinh }x=\\ln\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\right)$ for all $x$; $\\text{arcosh }x=\\ln\\left(x+\\sqrt{x^2-1}\\right)$ for $x\\geq1$. To solve $\\text{sinh}\\, x=k$ or $\\text{cosh}\\, x=k$ either use these or write in terms of $e^x$ and solve the resulting quadratic in $e^x$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "$\\frac{d}{dx}\\text{cosh}\\, x=+\\text{sinh}\\, x$ (no minus sign, unlike $\\cos$). $\\text{cosh}\\, x\\geq1$ always, so $\\text{cosh}\\, x=\\frac{1}{2}$ has no solution. Do not forget the $\\pm$ in the identity changes: $\\text{cosh}\\,^2x-\\text{sinh}\\,^2x=1$."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "Solve $\\text{sinh}\\, x=1$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\frac{e^x-e^{-x}}{2}=1$; put $u=e^x$: $u^2-2u-1=0$, $u=1\\pm\\sqrt2$.",
      "$e^x>0$ so $u=1+\\sqrt2$ and $x=\\ln(1+\\sqrt2)=0.881$."
     ],
     "answer": "$x=\\ln(1+\\sqrt2)\\approx0.881$",
     "figure": {
      "kind": "plot",
      "xmin": -3,
      "xmax": 3,
      "ymin": -5,
      "ymax": 5,
      "grid": 1,
      "w": 400,
      "h": 260,
      "curves": [
       {
        "expr": "(exp(x)+exp(-x))/2",
        "color": "blue",
        "label": "cosh x"
       },
       {
        "expr": "(exp(x)-exp(-x))/2",
        "color": "orange",
        "label": "sinh x"
       }
      ],
      "points": [],
      "segments": [],
      "xlabel": "x"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Evaluate $\\text{cosh}\\,(\\ln2)$ and differentiate $y=x\\text{cosh}\\, x$.",
     "steps": [
      "$\\text{cosh}\\,(\\ln2)=\\frac{2+\\frac{1}{2}}{2}=1.25$.",
      "Product rule: $\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\text{cosh}\\, x+x\\text{sinh}\\, x$."
     ],
     "answer": "$1.25$; $\\text{cosh}\\, x+x\\text{sinh}\\, x$"
    }
   ],
