   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Vector product",
     "md": "$\\vec a\\times\\vec b=(a_2b_3-a_3b_2,\\;a_3b_1-a_1b_3,\\;a_1b_2-a_2b_1)$. It is perpendicular to both $\\vec a$ and $\\vec b$, $|\\vec a\\times\\vec b|=|\\vec a||\\vec b|\\sin\\theta$ and $\\vec b\\times\\vec a=-\\vec a\\times\\vec b$. $\\vec a\\times\\vec b=\\vec 0$ if and only if the vectors are parallel."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "Areas",
     "md": "Area of the parallelogram on $\\vec a,\\vec b$ is $|\\vec a\\times\\vec b|$; area of triangle $ABC$ is $\\frac{1}{2}|\\vec{AB}\\times\\vec{AC}|$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "methode",
     "title": "Planes",
     "md": "A plane through a point with normal $\\vec n$ is $\\vec n\\cdot\\vec r=d$, i.e. $n_1x+n_2y+n_3z=d$. If you know three points $A,B,C$ use $\\vec n=\\vec{AB}\\times\\vec{AC}$. The distance from point $P$ to the plane is $\\frac{|\\vec n\\cdot\\vec p-d|}{|\\vec n|}$."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Common mistakes",
     "md": "The vector product is a VECTOR (the scalar product is a number). The order matters for the sign. Do not forget the middle component's order: $a_3b_1-a_1b_3$."
    },
